From: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: Copy the FDT into lowmem before unflattening it

The unflattened properties point into the blob. The boot loader may
place the blob high in RAM (in highmem), where reserved pages are not
saved in a hibernation image, and it rewrites the blob on the next
boot (e.g. bootargs). After a resume the properties would then point
at different data. Use unflatten_and_copy_device_tree().

Signed-off-by: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c b/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
index 0bfd66c7ada0..ada21432c834 100644
--- a/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
@@ -1163,7 +1163,15 @@ void __init setup_arch(char **cmdline_p)
 		register_restart_handler(&arm_restart_nb);
 	}
 
-	unflatten_device_tree();
+	/*
+	 * Copy the FDT into memblock memory (lowmem) before unflattening it.
+	 * The unflattened properties point into the blob.  The boot loader may
+	 * place the blob high in RAM (in highmem), where reserved pages are not
+	 * saved in a hibernation image, and it rewrites the blob on the next
+	 * boot (e.g. bootargs).  After a resume the properties would then point
+	 * at different data.
+	 */
+	unflatten_and_copy_device_tree();
 
 	arm_dt_init_cpu_maps();
 	psci_dt_init();
